<<~ aka "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/RFC-2119#/normative-language">>

<<^ code="&#x0002;">>

! Identity Classes ~ who runs, who carries, who rotates

> Status: PROPOSED — operator-ruled design (2026-07-20). The SUBSTRATE stands (the persona-root
> signs device-delegation edges; the guardian-card 2-of-3 + recovery-share type-wall + the charter's
> pre-rotated epoch chain all live). READING-B — recovery ROTATES rather than RESURRECTS — and the
> persona-KEL indirection it needs ride AHEAD of code.

A vessel wears a `#has`-stack, never a type ([[vessel-caps|lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/vessel-caps]]);
so an identity-CLASS reads the SAME way — a structural predicate over //what a principal runs, carries,
and how it recovers//, never a stamped tier. Four points in that space carry names because the mesh
returns to them: the ''USER'', the ''OPERATOR'', the ''KAHU'', and the ''HERM''. This meme maps them
across four axes and fixes how each RECOVERS — the axis Reading-B re-cuts.

<<~ ahu #/the-four-classes>>

!! The four classes ~ four axes

<<~ has Class USER "runs/NO infra (browser-style vessel) carries/short cap-stack · @oracle-read + own mesh-palace · a READ-CAP reaching its OWN operator's private data ACROSS the rhizome (relays blind-transit the ciphertext; the user decrypts) class/KERI non-transferable OR delegated recovers/abandon-and-recreate">>
<<~ has Class OPERATOR "runs/a node vessel carries/MANDATORY tier (@oracle + @crossroads + Kapae) · full VESSEL stack (tuber/bulb) · sovereign @catalog · BLIND-TRANSITS private ciphertext for the mesh (MLS Delivery-Service; carry ⊥ read) class/KERI transferable (its persona-KEL IS a key-event-log) recovers/recovery-root-authorizes-rotation (Reading-B)">>
<<~ has Class KAHU "runs/a node vessel — AND SEPARATELY holds a seat in the charter k-of-n (the vessel is layer ①, the seat layer ③; a seat moves without the vessel moving, and a vessel raises without the seat) carries/OPERATOR stack + the charter epoch chain + the steward repair-kit class/transferable, in TWO chains (own persona-KEL + the charter-KEL) recovers/personal (Reading-B) PLUS charter-quorum steward re-seat">>
<<~ has Class HERM "runs/the @daemon keel + own mesh-palace + own refresh clock (semi-autonomous relay) carries/MANDATORY public/infra + BLIND-TRANSIT of private CIPHERTEXT (carry ⊥ read; holds the replica, reads NONE) · NO read-cap on operator-content · NO sovereign @catalog class/NONE-CIVIC — holds a PLACE DID (the self-certifying key names a SOMEWHERE: addressable, vouchable, carriage-contractable) and NO operator DID (no human key rests at a crossroads to steal); authority rides a wax-sealed carriage contract recovers/re-established by its operator — no self-recovery of a civic identity it never holds">>

!!! ★ HERM READS AS A STATE EVERY VESSEL PASSES THROUGH, not only a class one vessel IS ★

''The four rows above name what a vessel STANDS AS once it holds its own keys. They do not name a fifth thing: where every vessel BEGINS.'' A node comes up at the waking floor — carrying, serving the public shelf, holding every sovereign act closed — and an operator ''lights the hearth fire'' by opening its archive. Until that act, an OPERATOR-class vessel and a HERM stand in the ''same state'', and naming them apart would freeze a difference that does not survive contact.

''So HERM reads two ways and both hold'': as a ''standing'' (a crossroads whose operator never intends to light it, contracted, faceless for good) and as a ''passage'' (any vessel, before its raise or after its raise lapses). The class rows describe the first; the floor describes the second.

''SEATED ⊥ RAISED keeps the class law intact through the passage.'' The Herm's zero persona-slot ceiling bars a ''SEATED'' persona root — a human's key RESTING on a crossroads. It bars nothing about a ''RAISED'' cap: those arrive WITH a recognised operator, ride that operator's own keys, and stop standing when the recognition stops. The at-rest state never changes, so a stolen disk still yields nothing of anybody's person, and a herm may grow a house without ever becoming a place that keeps one. <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/waking-floor">>

''And the floor is the HARDENED state, never a degraded one'' — the field inverted our first vocabulary, treating before-first-unlock as hardened and after-first-unlock as the liability. A vessel at the floor has lost its CAPS, never its FLOOR.

''The master cut runs AUTHORITY ⊥ FLOW'' (the cap-stack's, #vessel-caps): a USER carries little
authority and little flow; an OPERATOR carries sovereign authority AND heavy flow; a KAHU adds
//charter// authority atop the operator's; a HERM carries FLOW (carriage) with ''zero civic
authority'' — the one class that runs infrastructure yet holds no persona. Authority-to-run and
authority-to-BE separate cleanly at the Herm: it runs a full immune keel, and it //is// no ONE — yet
it //is// a SOMEWHERE. A Herm holds a ''PLACE DID'' and ''NO operator DID'' (operator ruling): the
crossroads earns a name it can be addressed and vouched by, while ''no local human key rests there to
steal''. ''Being-as-place ⊥ being-as-person'' — the Herm carries the first and never the second.

''And that claim holds at the CAP-STACK that made it, never at the box.'' A Herm that gains a
persona cap ''stops reading as a Herm'' — it composes into an operator-class vessel, and the
//nothing-to-steal// property leaves with the absent cap that carried it. This needs no check:
`composable-keel`'s ''absence = un-routed authority'' makes the boundary structural — //"a Herm
reads as a cap-stack that never declares the wiki cap… blind by structure, never by a flag a
later bug could flip"//. So a Lararium stacking a veiled key atop a Herm ''inherits the Place DID
and forfeits the claim'', by construction rather than by rule.

''A SECOND cut rides beneath the CARRIES column — TRANSIT ⊥ READ.'' What a vessel RELAYS
(transit/carriage, `sharePolicy`, advisory) never fuses with what it can DECRYPT (read/cap,
BeeKEM/CGKA crypto) — the carry-contract's carry ⊥ read law
([[carry-contract|lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/carry-contract]]#carry-read-contract). So the CARRIES
column reads on two lanes: the ''transit lane'' (which planes' bytes flow ACROSS this vessel) runs wide,
and the ''read lane'' (which planes this vessel decrypts) runs narrow. A Herm and a node Lararium both
BLIND-TRANSIT private ciphertext — they hold the encrypted replica and read NONE of it — while the
read-cap stays with the authorized decryptor alone. #the-mesh-breathes carries the mechanism.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-identity-class-ladder>>

!! The KERI ladder ~ transferable ⊥ non-transferable ⊥ delegated ⊥ none-civic

The class-axis reads KERI's identifier taxonomy, and the split draws by ''persistence and accreted
value'', never by title ([[founding-runbook|lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/founding-runbook]]#identity-classes):

* ''NON-TRANSFERABLE / basic'' (the USER floor) — a single-key identifier that pre-commits NO next
  key-set, so it ''cannot rotate by construction''. Its "rotation" reads as ''abandon-and-recreate'':
  mint a fresh identifier, drop the old. Cheap, native, no reserve, no guardians. The un-rotatability
  IS the property, not a lack.
* ''TRANSFERABLE'' (the OPERATOR spine) — a pre-rotated, persistent identifier that ''rotates its
  signing keys while its identifier prefix stays fixed''. Its key-event-log carries the rotation
  history; the charter's epoch chain reads as exactly this shape one scale up (#/the-continuity-anchor).
* ''DELEGATED'' (the USER's durable option) — an operator root ''delegates a disposable user stream'';
  durability lives in the ROOT, the leaf stays light and abandonable. A user gains persistence WITHOUT
  carrying a reserve (KERI delegated identifiers, KID0007).
* ''NONE-CIVIC'' (the HERM) — no identifier of ''persons'' at all. The self-certifying key that boots
  the keel stands as the Herm's ''PLACE DID'' — a somewhere, not a someone — and ''never an operator
  DID'': a crossroads holds no human key for a passer-by to steal. The operator's relation to it rides
  a wax-sealed contract-edge, never a delegated persona (#/herm-establishment).

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/promotion-path>>

!! The promotion path ~ value accretes, the class hardens

''What the ladder is a ladder OF'' — the drift below reads as `nohopapa`: dwelling in a realm deposits `papa`, and the accreted value IS the depth settled into. So the ladder never runs a rank assigned from above; it runs ''strata deposited by staying'', which is why it prices without ordering anyone against anyone. And the erosion runs the same way — stop dwelling and the depth wears down; no deed lapses, because none was ever granted.

''The Herm dwells in NO realm, and that follows from its facelessness rather than from a separate rule.'' Dwelling needs distinct loci of cost holding each other; a crossroads holds a Place DID and no human key, so nothing dwells there. It ''carries'' and never ''settles'' — the class stays structurally outside the dwelling plane, which is the same law that keeps it faceless.

An identity ''drifts UP the ladder as it accretes value it cannot cheaply re-mint'' — relationships,
standing, cabal entanglement (#the-frame carries the cost curve at founding-runbook#the-frame):

<<~moves user/non-transferable -> user/delegated -> operator/transferable on/accreted-value if/cheap-re-mint-no-longer-restores-the-relationships do/harden-the-class-not-the-person>>

* ''non-transferable → delegated'' — the light user, now worth keeping, accepts an operator root's
  delegation edge: the leaf stays disposable, the root carries the durability. No reserve lands on the
  user; recovery still reads abandon-and-recreate of the LEAF, re-delegated from the root.
* ''delegated → transferable'' — the vessel ''promotes'': it mints its OWN persona-KEL (an inception
  pre-rotation, #the-continuity-anchor), provisions the guardian-card reserve
  ([[charter-reserve|lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/api/charter-reserve]]), and steps off the root's
  delegation onto its own rotation chain. It becomes operator-class — it now carries the future.
* ''operator → kahu'' — a charter quorum SEATS the operator's key into the nexus k-of-n
  ([[charter-chain|lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/charter-chain]]); the operator gains a SECOND chain
  (the charter-KEL) atop its persona-KEL, and the steward repair-kit
  ([[siege-resilience|lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/siege-resilience]]#repair-kit).

The default holds: users stay light, operators carry the future — promotion moves by //grown value//,
never by decree.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/herm-establishment>>

!! Herm establishment ~ a contract, not a christening

An operator ''establishes a Herm by signing a Nexus carriage contract from a node vessel'', then leaves
it semi-autonomous (operator ruling, 2026-07-20). ''No civic identity mints into the Herm'' — only the
wax-sealed contract/edges:

<<~flows operator-node-vessel -> signs-carriage-contract (wax-sealed PEER/TRANSIT edge, MANDATORY tier) -> Herm-boots-own-@daemon-keel (self-cert PLACE DID + own refresh clock) -> semi-autonomous-relay>>

* the Herm ''boots permissionlessly'' on its own key (#vessel-caps: immune-core ⊕ blind-carriage ⊕
  public-read) — it asks no blessing to exist;
* the operator's authority over it rides the ''wax-stamped carriage contract''
  ([[wax-stamp|lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/charter-chain]]: provenance-of-the-data, not
  presence-of-a-person) — a frozen causal edge attesting //this operator carriage-contracted this Herm
  under epoch N//, never a live persona in the Herm;
* the Herm runs its OWN siege repair-kit at its OWN shrine tier (VSM recursion,
  #siege-resilience) — ''operational autonomy without civic identity''. It re-keys its soured leylines
  and heals its torn segments alone, yet holds no recoverable persona-root.

''So the Herm's autonomy and its recovery diverge.'' It self-heals its FLOW (segment repair) but never
self-recovers an IDENTITY — it holds none. A lost or soured Herm ''re-establishes from its operator'':
the operator re-signs the carriage contract and the Herm re-genesizes its keel from the bulb
(the engine-blob it already carries). The contract IS the whole authority relation; re-issuing it IS
the recovery.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-founding-splits>>

!! ★ A FOUNDING STANDS TWO THINGS — a PLACE, then a FACE ★

''A founding carries a SOMEWHERE and a SOMEONE, and canon keeps them apart.'' #herm-establishment rules it directly: a Herm ''boots permissionlessly on its own key — it asks no blessing to exist'', and ''no civic identity mints into'' it. A rite that minted a human root before a vessel could carry a byte would seat on every crossroads the one thing the class exists to refuse.

<<~ has Half Place "stands/@daemon · the vessel's own Keyhive individual · the hearth-true-name · the ContactCard asks/nobody ~ carries, serves the public shelf, holds every sovereign act closed">>
<<~ has Half Face "stands/the PersonaGroup + its private plane · the social planes · the device-delegation edge · the persona-KEL inception · the MeshCabal arrives/by an operator act ~ lights the hearth fire">>

''The place founds ALONE; the face lands on top of it, by a hand that came to dwell.'' A hearth whose operator stands right there runs both in one breath and gains nothing by typing twice. A crossroads never types the second at all.

!!! ★ THE CABAL RIDES WITH THE FACE ★

''A MeshCabal holds MEMBERS, and its members read as PersonaGroups.'' A cabal seeded on a place identifier would stand a membership structure with nothing that can be a member — so the cabal founds ''with the face'', seated on the group that can hold a seat in it.

''`IdentityAnchors` already files it that way'' — keyed by handle-index, the cabal id sitting beside the persona ids — and the boot path names cabal membership ''AFFILIATION, never identity'': a PersonaGroup belongs to many cabals or none (M:N), checked at ACCESS, local-first.

''A faceless place carries by CONTRACT instead.'' The wax-sealed carriage edge #herm-establishment already grants carries the authority a seat would have carried, so ''carry ⊥ read'' holds with no cabal anywhere.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-office>>

!! Kuleana ~ the OFFICE, and the civic standing between HERM and OPERATOR

''A civic lararium — a marketplace, a high temple, a district node with resident kahu — stands as none of the four rows above.'' It holds real operating authority, and it MUST hold no human's persona key at rest, because a hostile provider with disk access defeats every design that keeps one there.

''So it reads as a HERM THAT GAINED AUTHORITY CAPS WITHOUT GAINING A PERSONA CAP'', and `composable-keel`'s ''absence = un-routed authority'' makes that structural rather than flagged. Facelessness survives by construction.

<<~moves civic-standing -> derived-from/the-cap-stack on/every-read if/a-persona-cap-arrives do/stop-reading-as-civic>>

!!! ★ THE QUORUM SEATS THE OFFICE; THE QUORUM MUST NOT RENEW IT ★

''An office attaches to the PLACE, never to the person'' — the holder rotates through, the shrine keeps standing. And `attestation-plane` fixes which act a quorum gates:

> ''a quorum gates the rare, slow, high-power act, and automation carries the frequent, fast, low-power one. A quorum placed in the renewal path gets bypassed inside one outage, and the bypass becomes permanent.''

So the quorum ''seats'' (rare); the ''renewal rides the lease-epoch roll'' (frequent), which any writer advances in its own per-writer slot. The grant runs bilateral — a quorum countersignature over a subject naming the vessel's Place DID, requiring the vessel's own contract-in — and it ''ends by non-renewal''. Nobody exercises a lowering act.

!!! Two sources of caps, answering two layers

<<~ has Half Self-raise "layer/① act/open THIS vessel's archive holder/whoever holds this vessel's opening secret ~ bootstraps the first hearth; serves the portable node">>
<<~ has Half Office-grant "layer/③ act/a standing Nexus seats an office holder/any current office-holder opens it ~ no circularity: the Nexus already stands">>

''An office grant reaches NO archive by itself.'' A quorum's acts sit at ③, and a kahu holding shares becomes the collector the house forbids. The ① answer that survives: ''an OFFICE KEY, never a persona key'' — Place-DID-rooted, minted at establishment, opened through the raise door the mesh already stands. A human signs; ''never THE operator''. That difference carries the whole property.

''And the civic FLOOR runs far larger than a hearth's'': relay, public shelf, bulb, map-publish and segment-repair all stand with ''zero secret''. A district's service survives a power cut; only signing waits for a holder.

<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/lamplighters">> carries the Guild that tends these places, the immune coupling, and the tending caps.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-mesh-breathes>>

!! The mesh breathes ~ blind-transit of private ciphertext (carry ⊥ read)

''A Nexus breathes: private data flows ACROSS the relay infrastructure to reach its authorized reader,
and the relays read NONE of it.'' A Herm and a node Lararium both ''BLIND-TRANSIT private ciphertext''
— they hold the encrypted replica and forward its bytes toward the vessel that carries the read-cap,
which decrypts it alone. The relay carries; it never reads. This runs the node's canonical role: an
''MLS Delivery-Service'' — it delivers sealed group traffic, holding no group key.

The safety rests on the ''carry ⊥ read'' law, and it licenses carry to run GENEROUS:

* ''CARRY'' (`sharePolicy`, advisory) — the transit lane. Blind-transit of private ciphertext runs wide:
  the mesh breathes because relays forward sealed bytes freely.
* ''READ'' (BeeKEM/CGKA crypto) — the cap lane. A carried-but-uncapped doc reads `Key not found`; the
  read-floor is a causal-island-local FACT, not a policy (#/carry-contract).
* ''the gift'' — carry may be liberal ''because the read-floor catches every carry-mistake''
  (carry-contract#carry-read-contract): a generous transit tier never leaks a readable byte, the crypto
  the safety net beneath the routing. So a relay carrying a plane it must never read breaks no law — it
  cannot read it.

''This is how a user reaches its own private data remotely.'' A browser vessel of a recognized operator
stands FAR from the operator's node, yet reaches the operator's private data over the rhizome: the
relays blind-transit the ciphertext across the mesh, and the user — holding the read-cap by same-operator
grant (the device-fleet full-sync, already granted) — decrypts at the leaf. ''Transit crosses the whole
mesh; the read stays at the authorized vessel.''

''Two edges keep the breathing honest.'' First, the
''encrypt-first invariant'': blind-transit stays safe ONLY for what a plane seals for the mesh — a
cleartext-local plane a relay carried WOULD leak, so the self-slot's private-plane denial guards exactly
that gap. The discipline that makes the rhizome true reads ''everything that federates, encrypts first'';
seal it and carry-generous runs unconditionally safe, leave a plane cleartext-federatable and it names the
one hole. Second, ''content ⊥ metadata'': blind-transit seals what a relay READS, never what it SEES — the
shape of the flow (who ↔ whom, when, how much) crosses every relay. The mesh breathes ''content''-blind,
never ''metadata''-blind; traffic-pattern sovereignty rides a separate hardening (mixnets, cover traffic),
and the residual sits where canon already names it — the GPA-linkability bound, shape-provable only
(#/carry-contract). The choice architecture answers the rest: an operator who wants no relay to even SEE its
traffic simply does not contract those vessels into a Nexus — privacy rides the choice to contract, never a
wall built inside one.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/self-slot-reconciliation>>

!! Reconciliation ~ the committed self-slot vs the breathing mesh

The committed cross-operator self-slot ''DENIES a cabal-mate the private planes'' (`3f889b04` /
`7038224b`): a cross-operator presenting a valid self-cert card + a verified V3 proof rides a BOUNDED
federatable-carry tier — @crossroads + WHO + the Kapae antigen, the MANDATORY tier — and ''every private
plane (@catalog/@personal/@daemon/home/wikis) → DENIED''; a Kapae'd cross-operator draws Mu.

''No conflict at the READ lane.'' The denial that matters — a cross-operator MUST NOT decrypt another
operator's private data — stands untouched: the read-cap never crosses, the BeeKEM read-floor gates, and
the self-slot's own safety note already rests on ''carry ⊥ read'' (`7038224b`: "safety rides the
DeterministicFederationGate + the BeeKEM read-floor"). A user of the SAME operator gets the read-cap by
same-operator full-sync (already granted); a cross-operator never does. The self-slot protects the READ,
and Reading-1's blind-transit touches only the CARRY — orthogonal lanes.

''The fork rides at the CARRY lane — and it reads load-bearing.'' The committed `sharePolicy` denies the
private planes ''at the CARRY layer'' too: `7038224b` grants a cross-operator ONLY the federatable set,
so a cross-operator-CLASS relay currently ''carries no private ciphertext at all''. But the breathing
mesh (#/the-mesh-breathes) needs exactly that — a blind relay MUST transit private ciphertext it cannot
read, or the data never reaches its remote authorized reader across a foreign leg. So the committed
self-slot ''conflates carry-deny with read-deny for private planes'', and the mesh-breathes role needs
them split:

<<~ has Fork SELF-SLOT-A "keep/the committed posture — a cross-operator carries ONLY the federatable set, private ciphertext never transits a foreign relay cost/the mesh does NOT breathe across operator boundaries; a remote same-operator user reaches its private data only over IN-fleet legs, never a cabal-mate's relay">>
<<~ has Fork SELF-SLOT-B "refine/split sharePolicy's private-plane denial into DENY-READ-CAP (keep, absolute) ⊥ ALLOW-CARRY-of-ciphertext-to-a-blind-relay (new) — a cross-operator relay blind-transits sealed private bytes it can never read cost/a new carry-tier between MANDATORY and private-read; the relay holds encrypted replicas of planes it cannot decrypt (storage + the read-floor as the sole guard) gain/the mesh breathes — private data reaches its remote reader across ANY honest leg, carry-generous under the read-floor">>

''The recommendation leans SELF-SLOT-B'', because the mesh-breathes
role the operator named REQUIRES private ciphertext to cross foreign legs, and carry ⊥ read makes it safe
by construction — the relay holds bytes it provably cannot read. The refinement stays NARROW: it flips
the private-plane denial from ''deny-carry-and-read'' to ''deny-read, allow-blind-carry'', and changes
NOTHING at the read lane the self-slot was built to protect. ''Named as a fork'' because it edits a
committed security surface (`federation-gate.ts` `classifyCrossOperatorAdmission` +
`self-slot-share.ts` `selfSlotShareDecision`), and the operator owns that cut.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/reading-b-recovery>>

!! Reading-B ~ recovery rotates, it never resurrects

''Today (Reading-A) the persona-root IS the operational signing key'' — persona-vault vends "the
operator-root that signs edges", and the pinned `signerDid` every peer verifies against reads that
root's public key (ceremony-core: `signerDid = founderEdge.operatorDid`). Recovery reconstructs the
EXACT original root from a guardian quorum and re-signs a fresh device's edge with it
(recovery-core: the reconstructed root == the original). ''The old operational private key returns to
life'' — and the guardian quorum that rebuilds it holds, transiently, the whole signing authority,
forever, over anything (the recovery quorum IS the impersonation quorum, admitted as a priced/social
cost, [[persona-policy|lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/persona-policy]]#cryptographic-individual).

''Operator ruling (2026-07-20):'' a RANDOM recovery root authorizes a SIGNED recovery OPERATION rather
than resurrects the old operational private key. Recovery ''preserves identity continuity, not
cryptographic history.'' The move:

<<~moves recovery/reconstruct-then-resurrect-the-op-key -> recovery/attest-then-rotate-a-fresh-op-key on/an-independent-random-recovery-root if/continuity-anchors-on-the-identifier-not-the-key do/supersede-the-old-key-never-revive-it>>

Four parts carry it:

# ''The recovery root rides SEPARATE entropy'' — a random seed independent of the operational
  (persona-root) signing seed, exactly as the charter reserve's seed rides "a SEPARATE 32-byte CSPRNG
  seed — NEVER the live signing seed" ([[charter-reserve|lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/api/charter-reserve]]).
  A thief of today's operational key learns ''nothing'' about the recovery authority; a holder of the
  recovery authority signs ''only rotations'', never content.
# ''The identifier pre-COMMITS the recovery authority at founding'' — the persona's inception folds a
  DIGEST of the recovery root's authorized key-set (`charterKeySetHash`, already built), the same
  pre-rotation KERI commits for the charter (`nextKeyCommit`). The recovery keys never sign until the
  reveal; a compromise of the operational present cannot forge the recovery future.
# ''Recovery signs a ROTATION EVENT, not a re-admit of the old key'' — the recovery authority signs an
  event that (a) reveals against the pre-committed recovery-key digest, (b) SEATS a FRESH operational
  keypair the recovering vessel just minted, (c) marks the prior operational key retired, (d) hash-links
  onto the persona-KEL. This reads `rotateCharterEpoch` applied at PERSONA scale
  ([[wax-stamp|lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/charter-chain]]): reveal-the-pre-commit, seat-the-new-head,
  arm-the-next.
# ''The old key SUPERSEDES, never revives'' — the rotation advances the persona-KEL's head past the old
  operational key; a [[kapae|lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/kapae]] on the membership stack shadows its
  resurrection (evict runs forward-only, #siege-resilience). Post-rotation the fresh operational key sits
  SOLELY with the recovering vessel — no quorum, no guardian, no recovery root holds it. Continuity
  survives; the key-history turns over.

''Blast-radius, cut:'' Reading-A hands the recovery quorum the
operational key forever (sign anything). Reading-B hands it exactly ''one rotation'' — it can seat a
fresh key it does not itself hold, and nothing else. The recovery authority never becomes a content
signer.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-continuity-anchor>>

!! The continuity anchor ~ the persona-KEL, not the key

Reading-B ''requires an indirection today's stack lacks''. The Binding Gate pins `signerDid` == the
operational root's PUBLIC key and verifies every device-edge against that exact value; rotating the
operational key would break every pin. So continuity ''cannot ride the operational key'' — it must ride
a STABLE identifier the key rotates BENEATH.

''The persona gets its OWN key-event-log'' — a per-persona epoch chain the SAME shape as the charter's
(`CharterEpoch` + `verifyCharterChain` + `rotateCharterEpoch` ALREADY form a KEL; the persona-KEL reuses
the shape at persona scale). The invariant becomes:

* the ''identifier prefix'' — derived from the inception key-set + the pre-rotation commitment — stays
  FIXED across every rotation (the KERI autonomic-identifier / AID);
* a device-delegation edge pins the ''identifier'', and edge-verification WALKS the persona-KEL to the
  ''current'' authoritative operational key (latest-seen head wins, monotone-versioned);
* a rotation advances the head; the old edges still resolve, because they pinned the invariant
  identifier, never the rotated key.

''The load-bearing build for Reading-B read: give each PersonaGroup
a pre-rotated persona-KEL, and move the pin from the raw operational key to the identifier prefix.''
''BUILT'' — `persona-kel` mints the inception, derives the prefix, advances rotations hash-linked, and
verifies a chain; `boot-daemon-keyhive`'s Binding Gate pins the prefix and resolves the head. It lifted
the charter's proven epoch-chain machinery down to persona scale — invent nothing structural, re-site
what stands (#edges names the code shores). ''The same lift now runs OUTWARD'', to the two sites still
binding a raw key: the antigen's ban-nym and the handle-card's face-nym (#/the-honest-edges).

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-two-forks>>

!! The custody fork ~ reconstruct-then-sign ⊥ threshold-attest

The ruling fixes THAT recovery rotates; it leaves open HOW the recovery authority signs the rotation.
Two readings, one tradeoff axis — does the recovery authority EVER materialize as a single secret?

''FORK A — reconstruct-then-sign (guardians hold shares of the recovery root).'' The recovery ROOT seed
splits 2-of-3 across the shared guardian-card slots (mine/device + guardian-A + guardian-B), IDENTICAL
to the reserve ceremony — only the SECRET changes (the recovery root, never the operational root). At
recovery, two distinct custodians reconstruct the recovery root TRANSIENTLY, it signs ONE rotation
event, then zeroizes (`reconstructAndReadmit`'s window-bound, re-aimed at a rotation). ''Reuses the
entire guardian-card + recovery-share + reconstruct machinery almost unchanged.''

* //Tradeoff//: the recovery root still momentarily assembles as one secret — a transient
  impersonation-of-the-RECOVERY-authority window survives. It shrinks the blast radius (that secret can
  ONLY authorize a rotation, never resurrect the op-key or sign content), yet the recovery quorum stays
  AN impersonation quorum of the recovery authority.

''FORK B — threshold-attest (guardians each SIGN, no reconstruction EVER).'' Each guardian holds their
OWN independent recovery keypair; inception pre-commits the k-of-n digest of their recovery PUBLIC keys
(`charterKeySetHash`, the k-of-n cut already flagged in wax-stamp). At recovery, each guardian
independently SIGNS the rotation event with their own recovery key; the event carries k signatures
verified against the pre-committed set. ''No secret ever reconstructs — the strictest never-reconstruct.''

* //Tradeoff//: it does NOT reuse Shamir/recovery-share (a genuine k-of-n multisig over the persona-KEL
  rotation, small but new); it asks each guardian to mint + custody a keypair (heavier than "write down
  a card"); the rotation event carries k separate signatures. This reads the FROST/TSS direction
  recovery-core already gestures at ("the seed then never assembles").

!!! ⚠ What the outside sweep changed about this fork (2026-09-03)

A tasked spirit read the field (`docs/pono/recovery-custody-scout` carries it verbatim). Three findings move this section, and none of them picks the fork:

* ''EVERY civic-scale m-of-n in the world is SECRET SHARING'' — WebTrust defines it in //key shareholders// and //key shares//, the dominant CA HSM //re-creates// keys from K cards, IANA reassembles inside an HSM. ''Fork A is the shape the whole field runs''; Fork B has no civic-scale precedent to inherit.
* ''THE INVERSION.'' Fork A's assembled secret is a bearer token — courierable, delegable, improvisable — and that is ''simultaneously its worst security property and its best availability property''. ICANN held a key ceremony during a pandemic only because four key-holders could ''courier their credentials to surrogates''; under threshold signing that move is meaningless. ''Fork B cannot bend in either direction.''
* ''AND THE COUNTERWEIGHT.'' Independent-signature quorums are a ''DESTRUCTION quorum'', not merely an impersonation one: a rogue sub-quorum can emit a rotation nobody intended. Closable — but ''only by deriving the rotation body canonically'' rather than proposing it, and that mitigation belongs in whichever branch is taken.

⚠ ''Nothing in the public record turns on Shamir-versus-multisig.'' Every documented failure across the sweep turned on quorum counts that were not counts of distinct signers, correlated custody nobody re-checked, ceremony scripts diverging from reality undetected for months to years, guardians who forgot or folded, and vendors who left. ''The fork prices a risk the field has never been bitten by; the risks that bite are orthogonal to it.''

''Both satisfy the ruling'' — neither resurrects the operational
key; that part settled. The fork decides ONLY whether the RECOVERY authority itself ever briefly
materializes as one secret. The guardian-CARD survives either way — Fork A's card carries a share of the
recovery root; Fork B's card carries a guardian's recovery public key + a signing prompt. The operator
picks the axis: ''maximal reuse + a shrunk single-secret window (A)'' vs ''zero single-secret + new
multisig machinery and heavier guardian onboarding (B)''.

!!! ✓ RULED (operator, 2026-09-06) — the fork resolves as a LAYERED shape, not a winner

The forks answered different layers all along, and the ruling seats each where its shape fits:

* ''The NAME (the KEL prefix): FORK B'' — attest-then-rotate under the fixed identifier. ENACTED: no
  prefix incepts unarmed — every self-stood founding pre-commits the founder's 1-of-1 SELF-RECOVERY
  digest (`deriveSelfRecoveryKey`, a domain-separated leaf off the persona seed: the multitude-of-one,
  NAMED), and the self-rotation stands witnessed end-to-end (lose the device, hold the seed, rotate
  under the same name — `inception-armed.test.ts`).
* ''The MEMORY (the root seed / HD tree): FORK A as OPT-IN SELF-CUSTODY only'' — cards the human keeps
  or knowingly hands out. Never a default, never custodial, never the Nexus; every provisioning SAYS
  ALOUD that shares are keys. The silent-impersonation evil lives in DISTRIBUTING shares to other
  hands; self-escrow holds a quorum of one — the field's own courierability property, kept where it
  belongs.
* ''The CONTEST: FORK C, ON THE CHAIN'' — a recovery rotation enters the prefix's OWN KEL as
  PROVISIONAL and hardens causally. NEVER a pending-row on any board — a board of pending recoveries
  is a compiled registry of the vulnerable (the registry filter,
  `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/registry-filter`). The private VENUE is a guardian-cabal realm
  (the subject + their chosen guardians, ciphered): the realm coordinates, the chain hardens.

!!! ✓ THE HARDENING RULE — walked (2026-09-08), the φ-accrual half filled

Four clauses, each carrying its no-global-now discipline:

# ''A PROVISIONAL head confers only kapae-reversible authority.'' Until an observer hardens it, the
  fresh op-key performs ONLY acts whose supersession runs clean under remove-wins — re-standing the
  vessel, reading, presenting. It signs NO admission, NO burn, NO grant: exactly the act-set whose
  reversal costs nothing names the act-set a contested key may hold.
# ''The VETO out-competes causally, always.'' A competing event signed by the pre-provisional op-key
  supersedes the provisional wherever and WHENEVER it syncs — no window expires against an
  unpartitioned holder, because the contest is a causal fold, never a clock race. A veto arriving
  after some observer hardened still supersedes there; that observer's provisional-era state falls to
  kapae cleanup, which clause 1 guaranteed stays clean.
# ''Hardening is OBSERVER-LOCAL, by silence-across-K-local-epochs.'' Each gate accrues its own
  suspicion (the φ-accrual shape, made clockless): K of the OBSERVER'S OWN board-sync epochs advance
  with zero events from the prior op-key since the provisional entered — silence measured against
  local progress, never a wall clock. At the gate's own threshold, THAT gate treats the provisional
  head as head, full authority forward from its view. Gates harden at different causal moments and
  no agreement is needed, because clauses 1–2 kept safety independent of when anyone hardened. K
  rides per-gate policy; the end-user default runs generous.
# ''The board carries the CONTEST, never adjudicates it.'' Competing events at one seq demand
  contest-aware keying — `{prefix}/{seq}/{eventCid}`, never `{prefix}/{seq}` (a last-writer-wins
  slot would collapse a contest arbitrarily) — and the FOLD rule reads: a verified veto beats a
  provisional at the same seq, everywhere, always. An OPTIONAL Roughtime mark may stamp the
  provisional's mint as a bound-past for human reading; it never enters the fold.

''The G2 settlement this walk licenses:'' the persona-KEL's ONE remaining bytes-change adds exactly
the provisional marker and the veto kind (with the board keying above); nothing else rides it.
* ''CIVIC stays as wired'' — pre-rotation-with-reveal at the charter, the reserve-seed Shamir one
  layer beneath. The incumbent never generalizes upward.

''THE ROLLING COMMITMENT (enacted with the ruling):'' every KEL event carries `nextRecoverySetHash`
beside the genesis wall — the prefix keeps binding the GENESIS set (anti-swap survives), while each
rotation reveals against its predecessor's rolling commitment and GRAFTS the next. Guardian sets turn
over log-wise: 1-of-1-self → real hands → fresh hands when a guardian churns, each transition a
signed, board-walkable event. This retires the guardian-rotation gap without spending delegation.

''THE CROSSING RECORD (`reserve-transition` + `lares nexus seal grow`):'' when a multitude-of-one
becomes real hands, the old quorum signs the handoff, the new quorum countersigns the receipt (one
byte-image, the TUF cross-sign), and WITNESSES attest — where an independent witness is, checkably, a
key seated in NEITHER set. The record is carriage with the charter's own artifacts. The guardian CARD
split into TWO objects (a bearer SHARE vs a public REGISTRATION — own modules, own confirm domains,
own label stems), so the wrong object is not selectable: the ceremony-confusion cure the field earned.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-delegation-axis>>

!! ⚠ The axis that dominates the fork ~ delegation

> Under KERI's own rules, ''a non-delegated rotation cannot supersede another rotation''. So whichever fork is taken, ''a compromise of the recovery authority is TERMINAL unless the identifier is delegated''.

This is orthogonal to A-versus-B and larger in severity than either. The fork prices how briefly the recovery authority is exposed; ''delegation decides whether that exposure is survivable at all''. A recovery keel settled on the fork and silent on delegation has answered the smaller question.

Surfaced by the outside sweep (`docs/pono/recovery-custody-scout#the-third-axis`).

!!! ✓ MEASURED (2026-09-06) — and NOT SPENT

A research walk through KERI's own spec and kin systems priced delegation: a delegated inception
carries the delegator's AID INSIDE the prefix, permanently, with no severance mechanic — recoverability
purchased with a landlord in the identifier. The ROLLING COMMITMENT (#the-two-forks) answers the graft
without it: guardian sets turn over log-wise under the un-delegated prefix. What delegation alone would
have bought — superseding a compromise OF the current rolling set between grafts — narrows to the
contest window's job (Fork C: a provisional rotation the true holder out-competes causally). Delegation
stays REJECTED for the persona plane; a future entity that genuinely wants a standing superior (an
office, never a person) may revisit it under its own name.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-handle-chain>>

!! The Handle's chain ~ a SIBLING grammar, never an extension (walked 2026-09-08)

The nym's ruled chain (burn · re-key · public attestation) fits the persona-KEL's ''primitives'' and
not its ''grammar'', and forcing one grammar over both would couple what the ontology holds apart:

* ''Shared primitives:'' the hash-linked event core, the prefix-over-inception binding, the rolling
  recovery commitment (a Handle incepts ARMED like every prefix now does), the content-address
  discipline. One implementation family, reused.
* ''The handle-KEL's OWN kinds, absent from the persona grammar:'' an ''ATTESTATION'' event — a claim
  signed under the head ("this Handle controls `example.net`"), verified reader-locally against the
  claimed surface, carried ON the card per the registry filter — and a ''BURN'' — a terminal event
  after which no successor verifies, the Shadowtalk ending made structural.
* ''The OWNER-BINDING at inception:'' a Handle's inception carries its owning PERSONA-prefix, and the
  persona's KEL head authorizes handle rotations. This wears delegation's shape and pays none of its
  rejected price — the "permanent name inside the prefix" reads as a landlord on the persona plane
  and as the OWNER on the handle plane, because a Handle announcing whose face it is IS the
  bidirectional handle↔identity proof this canon already demands (#the-four-classes kin;
  `mesh/handle-card`). Burn authority rides the same binding: the persona buries its own name.
* ''Public by design:'' a handle-KEL diffuses wherever the card announces — the persona-KEL's
  per-Nexus board discipline does not govern it, and mixing the two grammars would have leaked one
  plane's diffusion posture into the other.

''So G2 splits clean:'' the persona-KEL freezes after the provisional/veto change; the handle-KEL
stands as a NEW sibling module (its own domain, its own kinds) with no bytes-change anywhere, built
in G3 on the frozen primitives.

!!! ✓ THE MU (operator, 2026-09-08) — a Handle is a QUORUM-presented name, not a lone key

''A cabal-realm and a public Handle carry ONE pattern integrity:'' a presentation reads VALID against
the current authority, and whether ONE or MORE humans hold the right to present it stays unknowable —
by design, exactly as a cabal refuses "which member signed". So the Dread Pirate Roberts was never a
succession MECHANISM; ''he is a Handle whose presenting authority is a QUORUM that grafts members'' —
Westley joins the presenting set, the old Roberts leaves, and the name reads continuously valid
because the presentation still satisfies the current quorum.

* ''The owner-binding generalizes'' from a single `ownerPrefix` to an OWNER-SET (persona-prefix
  members + a graft threshold), its digest folded into the prefix like the recovery set. ''1-of-1 is
  the degenerate case that IS the personal face'' — the same shape all the way down, no special
  civic tier.
* ''PRESENTATION (rotate · burn · attest) is authorized by ANY CURRENT MEMBER'' — you present as
  Roberts if you are a current holder. ''GRAFT (add/remove a member) is authorized by a THRESHOLD of
  the current set'' — the governance seam: a 1-of-1's sole willing hand, a guild's cabal quorum.
* ''Succession = grafting the presenting set via the rolling commitment ALREADY in the grammar'' —
  the prefix binds the GENESIS owner set (anti-swap: the name never moves), the rolling slot carries
  the CURRENT set. One signed graft event, cryptographic, no registry, no new persona bytes, ''no
  freeze spent'' (the handle-KEL is an in-flight sibling).
* ''It answers both kept kue'' — a civic name's cryptographic continuity (the graft IS the chain, no
  social hand-wave) and a crew resurrecting a name its holder can no longer cede (a k-of-n survives a
  lost member; the crew IS the quorum). The willing-cede residue shrinks to "a threshold of the
  current set consents" and routes to the human floor.

''This SUPERSEDES the cede-fork'' (was: new-kind-A ⊥ social-attestation-B): the answer is neither,
because succession was never a new thing — the name is a cabal, and the cabal grafts.

''THE FIELD NAMES BOTH FORMS'' (Deseriis, "improper names"; `api/pono/field-collision`): our
quorum-Handle is a STUDIED social form, not a novelty. A ''multiple-use name'' — an open name hundreds
present under, decentralized and idiosyncratic (Luther Blissett, 1994–99, VOLUNTARILY retired: a
deliberate succession) — is our k-of-n at large / the Dread Pirate Roberts. A ''collective pseudonym''
— a specific controlled group behind one name (Wu Ming) — is our chartered cabal. The vocabulary is
the field's; the mechanism (grafting the presenting set, identifier fixed) is ours.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-honest-edges>>

!! The honest edges (kept lit)

Three walls hold this design, and each stays named:

* ''The persona-KEL indirection STANDS — this wall came down'' (corrected; it read as an open gate long
  after it closed, and a stale wall misroutes every reader who trusts it). The Binding Gate ''pins the
  identifier PREFIX'' and walks the local KEL replica to its ''current head op-key''
  (`boot-daemon-keyhive` — a genesis-prefix mismatch, a broken or below-quorum head, or an edge that
  fails to chain each HALT fail-closed; `ceremony-core` records //"no raw-pin hybrid"//). So continuity
  ''rides the log, never a frozen key'', and Reading-B's rotation no longer waits on anything.
  ''What the indirection has NOT yet reached'' — two sites still bind a RAW key where a prefix belongs,
  and each carries a live consequence: the ''antigen'' bans a presenter `nym` (so a lawful rotation
  ''sheds the ban''), and a ''handle-card'' names a bare key as its `nym` (so a face carries no chain to
  break — hence no burn). Re-siting the KEL to both reads as the same lift persona-KEL itself performed
  on the charter machinery: //it invents nothing structural, it re-sites what stands//.
* ''"a valid rotation on lineage L" reads as crypto fact; "L is the legitimate person" does NOT'' — the
  same wall the wax-stamp and persona-policy keep lit. A rotation verifies against the pre-commit; that
  the recovering party //is// the original human stays higher-order social acceptance, answered by kahu-
  as-custodians and talk-story, never by a signature (#/persona-policy).
* ''the recovery-root pre-commit inherits the reserve's independence rule'' — the three recovery shares
  (Fork A) or the three guardian keys (Fork B) MUST sit in three domains that do not fall together
  (#founding-runbook: the online-identity trap + the co-location trap). A monoculture of custody defeats
  the rotation before it starts, exactly as correlated compromise defeats the refresh clock
  (#siege-resilience#cadence).

<<~/ahu>>

